# Headers for the paths the Worker never sees.
#
# Until 2026-09-07 `run_worker_first = ["/*", "!/assets/*"]` in wrangler.toml
# kept the hashed bundles on the asset server's fast path, and they skipped
# `harden()` in worker/index.ts — so this file was the bundles' ONLY `nosniff`.
# It is `run_worker_first = true` now (audit item 39): the negation was matched
# against the path, not against what existed at it, so a MISS under `/assets/`
# was the SPA fallback shell with no security headers and this file's year-long
# `immutable`. Every response now passes through `harden()`; the Worker still
# reads the bundles through the asset binding, which still applies this file,
# so the cache policy below is what a real bundle hit carries and `nosniff` is
# set twice. Both stay: Pages is the rollback and has no Worker.
#
# Do not reintroduce a negation, however narrow. A miss can be named anything.
#
# This is read as configuration by Workers static assets, the same way
# `_redirects` is — which is why `_redirects` cannot simply be deleted and has to
# be stripped from dist/ at deploy time. Unlike that file this one is valid for
# both hosts, so it needs no stripping: Pages applies it too, and Pages is still
# the rollback.
#
# The immutable cache header is safe only because these filenames carry a content
# hash: a changed file is a changed URL, so nothing can go stale.
/assets/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
